-- title:
--   Proposition 2.4 — $|V|$ and $|V_N|$ are bounded by $K_V$
-- statement:
--   Under Assumption 2.2 and the bound on $h$, the value functions of the infinite-horizon problem (2.14) and the finite-horizon problem (2.15) are finite, and
--
--   $$
--   |V|,\ |V_N|\ \le\ K_V:=\frac{K_f}{r}+\frac{4TMK_h}{1-p_2},
--   $$
--
--   where $K_f=\max_{\bar Q}|f|$ and $M,p_2$ are as in (A.2). Here $V$ is taken on $\bar Q$, and $V_N(t,x)=\tilde V_N(t,t-\lfloor t\rfloor_T,x,1,0)$ for $N\ge1$, $t\in[0,NT]$, $x\in\mathcal O$, with $\lfloor t\rfloor_T=T\lfloor t/T\rfloor$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: bounded smooth domain → open, connected, bounded, with a global $C^\infty$ defining function $\rho$; reason: equivalent for bounded domains; the paper gives no degree of smoothness, read as $C^\infty$
--   - encoding: $f$ uniformly Hölder on $\bar Q$ with exponent $\alpha$ → Hölder for the metric of $\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^d$ with an existential $\alpha\in(0,1]$; reason: with $\alpha$ existential this and the parabolic Hölder class coincide on the bounded set $\bar Q$
--   - reading: $d$-dimensional balls, open or closed not specified → open balls; reason: the two readings agree, since $\varepsilon$ is arbitrary and balls can be slightly enlarged
--   - reading: measurability of $(t,x)\mapsto\nu_{t,x}$ with respect to the weak convergence topology → Borel for the topology of `FiniteMeasure` on $Q$; reason: this is the direct meaning of the phrase
--   - encoding: the process $(v,X)$ with $\theta_{i+1}=\inf\{s>\theta_i: X_{s-}\in\partial\mathcal O\text{ or }v_{s-}=T\}$ on a fixed filtered space → any `Realization`: the filtered space is part of the data, $\theta_{i+1}$ is the end of a cycle in $Q$ with left limit in $\partial_pQ$, stochastic integrals are `HasItoIntegral`, the conditional law is given $\mathcal F_{\theta_i-}$ with $\mathcal F_{\tau-}$ generated by the sets $A\cap\{s<\tau\}$; reason: same object: first hit written without an infimum of a possibly empty set; Mathlib has no $\mathcal F_{\tau-}$
--   - encoding: $f(v_{s-},X_{s-})$ and products over $\theta_j$ in $Y$ → $f(v_s,X_s)$ under $ds$ and `finprod`; reason: the left limit differs from the value at jump times only, a Lebesgue null set; only finitely many $\theta_j$ lie below $s$ almost surely
--   - generalization: $|h(s,x)|\le K_h\cdot s$, (2.16) → $|h(s,x)|\le K_h\cdot T$ on $\partial_pQ$; reason: (2.16) implies this bound because $s\le T$, and the proofs use only this bound (p.23)
--   - encoding: the expectation in the statement → integrability of the functional is asserted explicitly; reason: the paper's expectation presupposes it; without it a Bochner integral defaults to $0$
--   - reading: $p_2$ and $M$ as defined in (A.1) → one existential $M\ge1$, $p_2\in(0,1)$ binding (A.2) at the model's rate and the bound; $p_2$ may be larger than the printed one; reason: the page's constants are not explicit; a start on $\partial_pQ$ adds one term $K_hT$, which a larger $p_2$ absorbs
--   - encoding: $V(t,x)$, $V_N(t,x)$ as functions → the bounds hold for the expectation under every realization started at $(t,t,x)$; reason: the process is given through realizations
--   - encoding: $V_N(t,x,y)=\tilde V_N(t,t-\lfloor t\rfloor_T,x,y,0)$ → $y=1$, $\lfloor t\rfloor_T=T\lfloor t/T\rfloor$; reason: the notation $V_N(t,x)=V_N(t,x,1)$ of p.10; $\lfloor t\rfloor_T$ is the largest integer multiple of $T$ not above $t$
-- source:
--   Dai, Kou, Yang, A Stochastic Representation for Nonlocal Parabolic PDEs with Applications, SSRN 3541591, Proposition 2.4, p.10

import Definitions.Def_NonlocalFK_Realization

open MeasureTheory Set Filter

universe u

namespace NonlocalFK

/-- Proposition 2.4 (Dai, Kou, Yang, SSRN 3541591, p.10): under Assumption 2.2 and the bound on `h`,
`|V|` and `|V_N|` are bounded by `K_V := K_f/r + 4TMKₕ/(1 − p₂)`, with `M`, `p₂` as in (A.2).

**Formalization Note.** `V` and `V_N` depend a priori on a realization, so the statement is about
every realization: `V` on `Q̄`, as in (2.14), and `V_N(t, x) = Ṽ_N(t, t − ⌊t⌋_T, x, 1, 0)` for
`N ≥ 1`, `t ∈ [0, NT]`, `x ∈ 𝒪`, as in (2.15), i.e. under every realization with real start `t` and
clock start `t − ⌊t⌋_T`, where `⌊t⌋_T = T⌊t/T⌋`. `M` and `p₂` are
existential and bind (A.2) and the bound together; `K_f = max_{Q̄} |f|`. -/
theorem proposition_2_4 {d : ℕ} (m : Model d) (hS : m.Standing) (h22 : m.Assumption22) :
    ∃ M : ℕ, 1 ≤ M ∧ ∃ p₂ : ℝ, 0 < p₂ ∧ p₂ < 1 ∧
      (∀ n : ℕ, ∀ p ∈ m.Q, ∀ (Ω : Type u) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (R : Realization m 0 p.1 p.2 Ω),
        ∫ ω, Real.exp (-m.r * R.θ (4 * n * M) ω) ∂(R.P) ≤ p₂ ^ n) ∧
      ∀ Kh Kf : ℝ, m.Growth Kh → IsGreatest ((fun p => |m.f p|) '' m.Qbar) Kf →
        (∀ p ∈ m.Qbar, ∀ (Ω : Type u) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (R : Realization m p.1 p.1 p.2 Ω),
          R.PayoffIntegrable ∧
            |∫ ω, R.payoff ω ∂(R.P)| ≤ Kf / m.r + 4 * m.T * M * Kh / (1 - p₂)) ∧
        (∀ N : ℕ, 1 ≤ N → ∀ t ∈ Icc 0 (N * m.T), ∀ x ∈ m.O, ∀ (Ω : Type u) [MeasurableSpace Ω]
          (R : Realization m t (t - m.T * ⌊t / m.T⌋) x Ω),
          Integrable (R.finitePayoff N) R.P ∧
            |∫ ω, R.finitePayoff N ω ∂(R.P)| ≤ Kf / m.r + 4 * m.T * M * Kh / (1 - p₂)) := by sorry

end NonlocalFK
